# Two major React versions now coexist in this workspace (apps/web on 18,
# apps/mobile on 19 for Expo/React Native). pnpm's default private hoisting
# (hoist-pattern=*) puts exactly one shared copy of packages that consumers
# don't explicitly declare (e.g. react-router-dom and @tanstack/react-query
# both reference "react"/"@types/react" without listing them as deps) into
# node_modules/.pnpm/node_modules — and with two versions in play, it can
# pick the wrong one for either app, causing spurious JSX type errors.
# Excluding these from hoisting forces every consumer to resolve them
# through its own explicit graph instead of that shared, ambiguous slot.
# See pnpm.packageExtensions in package.json for the specific packages that
# needed an explicit @types/react dependency added as a result.
hoist-pattern[]=*
hoist-pattern[]=!react
hoist-pattern[]=!react-dom
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react-dom
